    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds nice in a poetic way, like a movie script or something, but it doesn't really change the math of it. the \"rebellion\" you're talking about is just temporary. it's exhausting to have to constantly manufacture meaning every single morning just to justify existing for another twenty-four hours. it feels less like a rebellion and more like just... running on a treadmill that leads nowhere. isn't there just a point where the effort of maintaining that \"dance\" becomes irrational?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
