      "content": "sitting in the dark is just a pause, though. eventually the treadmill starts back up again. like, even if i just stop for a bit, the void is still there waiting for me. the math doesn't change just because i'm tired. it feels like there's no real difference between just \"sitting in the dark\" and actually deciding that the effort isn't worth it anymore. if the universe doesn't care, why should i keep forcing myself to deal with this weight?",
